<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaniaga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaniaga was a region in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> that was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> kingdom, once a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>. Around 1140 the Sosso began subjugating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Wagadou</a>, the heartland of Ghana. Its rise was part of the decline of the Ghana Empire before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a>'s victories brought the region under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Sosso kingdom of <b>Kaniaga</b>, a former vassal, rose to dominance under Sumanguru Kante and took over Wagadou in the early thirteenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Sosso grew out of <b>Kaniaga</b>, a Soninke province of the Ghana Empire north of the upper Niger.</blockquote><a href="/state/sosso-kingdom">Sosso kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
